        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Edits the caller/callee graph with state info from &apos;ini&apos; :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. note::
   The base implementation forwards straight to #edit and **ignores &apos;ini&apos; entirely**,
   exactly as the pure-Python original does (its ``BaseIniPartEdit.editFromIni`` calls
   ``self.edit(*args, **kwargs)`` without passing ``ini`` along). Subclasses that
   actually need the ``.ini`` file&apos;s state override this rather than #edit
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>graph</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The graph to edit, modified in place </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ini</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The associated .ini file. <bold>Nullable</bold> <ndash/> see this subsystem&apos;s own note on still-pure-Python collaborators </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of mod to fix. <bold>Nullable</bold>, same reason </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the mod to fix to. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>""</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>partFilter</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The filter for valid order indices <ndash/> empty for &quot;no filter&quot;. <bold>Default</bold>: empty </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>trackKeys</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The caller&apos;s key-tracking default <ndash/> see <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_base_ini_graph_edit_1ad62d6a67c4e3f2e6de43349d732a8fa9" kindref="member">edit</ref>. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>keysToTrack</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The caller&apos;s key-tracking key set <ndash/> see <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_base_ini_graph_edit_1ad62d6a67c4e3f2e6de43349d732a8fa9" kindref="member">edit</ref>. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The same graph that was passed in, after editing </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
